  "reference": {
    "title": "Reference",
    "lead": "An engineer's cheat sheet: fits with a tolerance calculator, steel grades, GD&T symbols, surface roughness and welds. Values are typical; always check the standard for exact figures.",
    "fits": "Fits and tolerances",
    "fitsLead": "ISO 286. Pick a nominal size and tolerance classes and the diagram updates. In notes, write `H7/p6` or `Ø25 H7/p6` to get a tooltip.",
    "steels": "Steels and alloys",
    "steelsLead": "Grade, standard, foreign equivalents, strength and typical use. In notes, `40Х` or `Сталь 45` gets a tooltip.",
    "gdt": "Geometric tolerances",
    "gdtLead": "ISO 1101 / ГОСТ 2.308. A tolerance sits in a frame: symbol, value in mm, then datum letters.",
    "frameExample": "Examples: perpendicularity 0.02 mm to datum A; position Ø0.1 mm to datums A and B.",
    "datum": "needs a datum",
    "noDatum": "no datum",
    "roughness": "Surface roughness",
    "roughnessLead": "ГОСТ 2789-73 / ISO 21920. Ra in µm is the usual parameter. Old Soviet roughness classes still show up in textbooks, so they are listed too.",
    "ra": "Ra, µm",
    "rz": "Rz, µm",
    "oldClass": "Class",
    "method": "Typical process",
    "use": "Where it's needed",
    "welds": "Welds",
    "weldsLead": "ГОСТ 5264-80 (manual arc welding) and ГОСТ 2.312-72 (symbols). A weld code is the joint letter plus the preparation number, e.g. «ГОСТ 5264-80-Т1-⊿6».",
